ient-specific factors in drug selection and safety [Data: Entities (2617, 14910); Relationships (19970, 7120)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Adverse reactions link drugs to ophthalmic and metabolic side effects\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Several drugs are associated with notable adverse reactions beyond cardiovascular effects. 地高辛 is linked to 弱视 (amblyopia or visual impairment) as a potential toxicity symptom, consistent with known digitalis toxicity manifestations. Separately, 环孢素 is associated with 糖耐量异常 (impaired glucose tolerance), a metabolic disturbance that can predispose patients to diabetes. These findings illustrate the multisystem impact of pharmacotherapies and the need for comprehensive monitoring [Data: Entities (15920, 16775); Relationships (10579, 13966)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Drug–drug interactions pose clinically significant risks\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Multiple documented drug–drug interactions highlight potential for altered efficacy or toxicity. For instance, 乌拉地尔 interacts with 西咪替丁, leading to a 15% increase in 乌拉地尔 blood concentration, which could amplify hypotensive effects. Similarly, Ⅰ类抗心律失常药 interact with 美托洛尔, potentially prolonging cardiac conduction and increasing arrhythmia risk. Additionally, 单硝酸异山梨酯缓释’s hypotensive effect is enhanced when combined with 三环类抗抑郁药. These interactions necessitate careful polypharmacy management, especially in complex patients [Data: Entities (3396, 3989, 10103, 7286); Relationships (27483, 31217, 26816)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Non-pharmacological factors like diet influence key health indicators\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Dietary components such as 膳食纤维 are recognized as modulators of blood pressure, indicating that non-drug interventions also play a role in this community. While the primary focus of the network is pharmacological, the inclusion of 膳食纤维 reflects an integrative view of healt